Z||000011||BAM-BAM||07-02-2000||10:59 PM||||  Spike, I would seriously think about what you are about to do to your Fiero. I realize that everyone has their own likes and dislikes, but you have no idea how many toes you are about to step on. I had a 67 Bronco with the fender flares you are talking about. It looked good. To even consider putting those flares on a Fiero is an outright sin; unless of course you plan on cruising the swamp lands of Louisiana or perhaps the Florida everglades. Please consider an IMSA style makeover first. <P>  Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. Just my opinion   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mvc-167fm.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mvc-169fm.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mvc-166fm.jpg"> <BR> Do you see what I am talking about?<BR>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 07-02-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000012||stimpy||07-02-2000||11:14 PM||||Real cheap fix... find some of those treads that come off of semi trucks. They are relatively easy to find and they are FREE! Trim them to fit and sheet metal screw them to the wheelwells.  For a custom "glassed-in" look, you can caulk it with bath tub caulking. I say go for it, opinions be damned! It's your car, and you'll probably never want to sell it anyway!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
